=== 5. Decision Matrix: Which Results to Report ===

Every scenario below is adjudicated '''together with the scatter and funnel plots''' ([[#3.5 Visual Diagnostics: Scatter and Funnel Plots|§3.5]]): visual identification of outlier SNPs or funnel asymmetry can select MR-PRESSO or an Egger/mode model even when the numeric trigger (Cochran's ''Q'', the Egger intercept) is borderline. Record the model used and the visual rationale per association.

{| class="wikitable"
! Scenario !! Data Presentation !! Adjudicated Result to Report
|-
| '''1. Clean Signal''' || F > 10. Cochran's Q p > 0.05. Egger Intercept p > 0.05. CAUSE Causal Model p < 0.05. || "IVW (Fixed Effects). All assumptions are met."
|-
| '''2. Balanced Pleiotropy''' || F > 10. Cochran's Q p < 0.05 '''or''' one/few outlier SNPs visible in the scatter/funnel (§3.5). Egger Intercept p > 0.05. || "MR-PRESSO (Outlier Corrected) or IVW (Random Effects). Support with Weighted Median."
|-
| '''3. Weak Instruments''' || Mean F < 10 OR Relaxed criteria (p < 5e-6) used. || "MR-RAPS. Baseline IVW is vulnerable to weak instrument bias."
|-
| '''4. Directional Pleiotropy''' || Egger Intercept p < 0.05 '''or''' clear funnel asymmetry (§3.5). || "Weighted Mode (if I2GX < 0.90) OR MR-Egger Slope (if I2GX >= 0.90). IVW is discarded."
|-
| '''5. Correlated Pleiotropy''' || CAUSE model comparison p > 0.05 (Sharing Model wins). || "Null Result (Discard Causality). The traits are correlated due to shared genetics, not a direct causal pathway."
|-
| '''6. Inconclusive''' || MR-PRESSO removes >30% of SNPs causing power loss, OR Median and Mode significantly contradict each other. || "Unresolved / Inconclusive. State that genetic evidence is too pleiotropic to reliably disentangle."
|-
| '''7. Selection/collider bias''' || Both arms present AND predicted bias same sign as observed AND predicted ≈ observed magnitude. || "Report as selection-bias-consistent, not causal. Give uncorrected + corrected estimates."
|}

